A||||9||wkayl||STILL no spark||||8||
Z||000000||wkayl||09-26-2001||09:31 PM||||Stopped at Wal-Mart last week.  Came out and wouldn't start!  Had my wife pick me up.  2 hrs later went to drag it home.  It started right up.  Today I backed it into driveway.  Replaced a cracked vacume line.  Now no spark again!  I replaced all connectors to coil and dist.  Replaced ign. module (had old one tested at Auto Zone-checked OK).Replace coil wire.  I swapped coils from my "running" GT.  Still no go. This is on the 88 Formula.  <P>Whoever can give me the answer to correct my problem, I will send a copy of the bootlegged video of the birth of the Fiero I payed way too much for on E-bay (poor quality and all).  <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/usa1017[1].gif">   <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||8
Z||000001||87GTZ34||09-26-2001||10:00 PM||||Ya know...  I had the same problem with intermittant spark.  It turned out to be the 2-wire connecting harness between the distributer and the coil.  Alex4mula also had the other distributer harness give him intermittants.  It is a pain in the a$$ as it runs, it doesn't run.  I finally got ticked one day and wiggled all of the distributer harnesses and viola, it started.  H-m-m-m-m  $34 later I had no more problems.  Hope this helps.  Let me know if I win...  GL & I hope this helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-26-2001||11:15 PM||||check over C500. Coil power runs thru there. That's the huge block by the battery.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||MooCow||09-27-2001||01:15 AM||||On my 87 GT it died on me one day and then when I went to start it again it started right up like yours did and then died again.  For me it was the ignition modual at first.  Then the pick-up coil inside the distributor went out.  Make sure you plugged in everything right.  Also see if you have spark off the coil or not.  Good luck to ya.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierogtracer||09-27-2001||03:12 AM||||One quick question. Do you have a multimeter?<BR>If so I can tell you the places to test to tell exactly what it is.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_11.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||wkayl||09-27-2001||09:42 AM||||All good suggestions so far.  I replaced the 2 wire connector between the coil and dist.  I have 12 volt power to the coil.  I am checking the spark directly out of the coil.  I have replaced the Dist.  I have checked the pickup coil in dist. with multimeter.  I even checked the ECM fuse in the fuseblock (one of the last things a guy would think of). This evening I will check the power block by the battery.  I have wiggled those wires, but havn't disconnected them and checked for breaks.  Good thing I still have some hair left on my head.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||OcalaFiero||09-27-2001||09:58 AM||||Try checking the electrical connections at the coil, distributor, and also check the tach filter. Also check to make sure there are no shorts from your plug wires to the motor. Check the ignition switch (down on the bottom of the column) also, that was a problem I came across in mine. <P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<BR>'86 2M4<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallsigpic_1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by OcalaFiero (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||wkayl||09-28-2001||06:26 PM||||Ok, here is the latest.  I thought I had it when I checked the battery junction block suggested by theogre.  I found a fusable link that when i touched it something would hum for a few seconds over by the air filter (don't know what that was).  I repaired the wire but it still wouldn't start.  This morning I went out and hit the key.  It turned over a few times and then "BANG" out the exhaust and it started up.  I started it up about 4 times, moved it over to the side of the driveway so I could get my GT out.  I shut it off and tried to restart it.  No go again.  Just cranks.  I bought a can of starting fluid (I know, I'm desperate) to make sure it wasn't a fuel problem.  Still no go.  I have had many good suggestions here, keep them coming.  Even the most obvious (clean connectors, everything plugged in) are appreciated.  It may just be something silly like that||||reg||1
Z||000008||JetroGT||09-28-2001||06:52 PM||||Replace the modual under the cap. 20 dolar part. I suggest getting the GM part because it lasts alot longer, but it's more expensive.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">  <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.<BR>Wanted: 86/87 Red GT, auto, pw, pl, pm, rear defrost,pt, Gray int, Spoiler. May be willing to trade the blue car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrfiero||09-28-2001||10:37 PM||||Wayne,<P>Will you be around this weekend?  Since I'm in Greeley now driving to Loveland is no big deal.  I could come over and help figure it out.<P>LMK......I'll PM you my phone #.||||reg||1
